a.common('Build a baseline for a different catalogue','Validate inputs, apply every fitting condition and the stated order, and record actual results under a shared comparison contract.',[(12,'W1 · State the complete activity requirements','Use the supplied catalogue and explain the quiet condition precisely.'),(13,'W2 · Run three baseline requests','Show the output and deciding checks for each.'),(14,'W3 · Distinguish blank from valid zero','Explain clarification versus a genuine no-match result.'),(16,'W5 · Plan a fair baseline/prototype comparison','Use the same requests, catalogue and judging rules, and retain all results.')], 'For the two-design paper audit, the name field changes no compatibility result and is unnecessary for this task. Using the activity catalogue: (12,No) returns B1, first among multiple fitting options; (8,Yes) is a valid no match because B2 is not quiet and other activities exceed 8 minutes; (blank,Yes) needs clarification; (0,Yes) is valid but has no match. Preserve the distinction between missing input and no fitting row. Matching correct outputs establishes agreement on these cases, not speed, usability or universal reliability. Provide the full activity catalogue before the lab. Reserve Build a baseline for a different catalogue for the independent first attempt.',{12:[r]})
